WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.569
Director Matt Reeves' The Batman may not have
Ben Affleck rocking the cape and cowl anymore,

00:00:05.569 --> 00:00:09.080
but what it does apparently have are two main
villains plucked straight from the Batman

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.220
canon the second of which may have just been
revealed.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.970
A casting breakdown for The Batman, obtained
by We Got This Covered through undisclosed

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:21.619
sources, reportedly details that the secondary
baddie in the film is a character currently

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.000
being billed as "The Brain."

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.919
There's a villain who goes by that name in
the DC universe: a mad scientist best known

00:00:27.919 --> 00:00:32.500
for serving as a member of the Brotherhood
of Evil, joining the Secret Society of Super

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.960
Villains, and battling against the band of
crime-fighting misfits known as the Doom Patrol.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:42.030
It would be an interesting choice for a central
antagonist in a more noir-driven, detective

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:47.040
version of Batman — especially considering
the Brain and Batman aren’t exactly arch-enemies.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.320
Of course, it’s entirely possible that the
Brain isn’t the secondary villain in the

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:56.000
forthcoming film after all, but simply a code
for a different super-villain set to battle

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:56.500
Batman.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.060
“Surf’s up, big Kahuna!”

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:05.100
According to We Got This Covered’s intel,
"the Brain" is actually code for a far more

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.640
prominent DC Comics villain: the Riddler.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:11.939
As avid Batman readers will know, the "Brain"
could here be a reference to the fact that

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.820
the Riddler is Batman's most intelligent arch-villain.

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:20.140
Otherwise known as Edward Nigma, The Riddler
possesses genius-level smarts and revels in

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.460
crafting dastardly plots that involve complex
riddles, traps, and puzzles.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.520
Showy, over-elaborate, and weirdly passionate
about the crimes he commits, the Riddler has

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:33.799
long existed as one of Batman's greatest and
most notorious adversaries.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.820
"What squeals louder than a caught rat?”

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.720
“Answer... several caught rats."

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.540
What makes the Riddler’s presence in the
Reeves-helmed flick even more plausible is

00:01:45.549 --> 00:01:50.390
that the primary bad guy of The Batman is
reported to be the Penguin., this Gotham City

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:54.320
mobster has a flair for the dramatic and a
penchant for all things avian.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.670
A team-up between the two villains wouldn’t
be too out of the ordinary, either, since

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:02.420
the Penguin has frequently partnered with
the Riddler, both on-screen and off.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:06.520
While the Fox television series Gotham has
depicted both the Riddler and the Penguin

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:11.430
throughout the show's run, neither villain
has appeared on the big screen since the 1990s.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:16.000
Tim Burton's Batman Returns featured Danny
DeVito as the Penguin, while Joel Schumacher's

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:21.140
1995 feature Batman Forever saw Jim Carrey
give an over-the-top performance as the Riddler.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:22.600
“Thank you.”

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:27.959
Some might argue that Carrey and DeVito were
perfect — and maybe even irreplaceable — in

00:02:27.959 --> 00:02:32.980
their roles, but it's been over 25 years since
the release of Batman Returns and Batman Forever,

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:36.980
and the Riddler and the Penguin are long overdue
for a silver screen face lift.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:40.700
Reeves' movie could be the perfect platform
to do just that.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.560
Obviously, it goes without saying that this
is all guesswork for now.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:48.691
No one directly involved with The Batman has
confirmed that the Riddler will be a part

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:52.720
of the story, and nobody has corroborated
the talk that the Penguin will appear, either.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:56.940
Nonetheless, this rumor does seem just about
plausible enough to be true — and it can

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:01.099
only help that the Riddler has already found
his roots in the DC Extended Universe, thanks

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:05.200
to a sneaky little Easter egg in Batman v
Superman: Dawn of Justice.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.680
Until someone finally steps up and confirms
The Batman’s lead villains, however, fans

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:14.640
are just going to have to count down the days
until the film releases on June 25th, 2021.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:19.680
Of course, if that gets too boring, they could
always pass the time by fan-casting the Riddler.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:21.000
Our money's on DiCaprio.

